  "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented payment terms functionality. Here's a summary:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n**Updated: `src/errors.js`**\n- Added `TERMS_INVALID`: \"Payment terms must be 'NET14', 'NET30', or 'EOM'.\"\n\n**Updated: `src/invoices.js`**\n- Added import of `addDays` from dates.js\n- Added internal `calculateDueDate()` helper function that:\n  - NET14: adds 14 days to issue date\n  - NET30: adds 30 days to issue date (default)\n  - EOM: calculates last day of the issue date's month\n- Modified `createInvoice()` to:\n  - Accept optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n  - Validate terms before validating lines\n  - Calculate `dueDate` based on terms\n  - Return `TERMS_INVALID` error for unknown terms\n  - Include `terms` and `dueDate` in the returned invoice object\n\n**Updated: `test/invoices.test.js`**\n- Added 13 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Default NET30 behavior\n  - NET14 and NET30 terms\n  - EOM calculation for various dates (Feb leap year, month boundaries, year wrap)\n  - Due date calculations that cross month and year boundaries\n  - Error handling for invalid terms\n  - Validation order (terms validated before lines)\n  - Terms preservation through invoice operations\n\n**Test Results**: All 148 tests pass (135 existing + 13 new)\n\nThe implementation correctly handles all term types, edge cases like leap years and month boundaries, and validates terms early in the invoice creation process.",
